DESCRIPTION:The Bloomington Symphony Orchestra sponsors an annual competiti
 on among the best music students in the area. Students work with their teac
 hers to select and prepare a solo piece\, then perform it for members of th
 e BSO. We then award the top performers a scholarship and arrange for them 
 to play their chosen piece as a soloist with the BSO during our regular con
 cert season. Violinist Joshua Bell was one of our first winners! \nThe next
  round of auditions will be held on November 7\, 2026\, and that the winner
  will have a chance to perform with the BSO during our March 7\, 2027 conce
 rt. \nApplications are due October 24\, and auditions will be November 7\, 
 2026\, 10am-2pm at Faith Lutheran Church.\nVideo auditions will be accepted
  only in case of a scheduling conflict. \nFor all rules of participation\, 
 and the application Click Here.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260925T194628Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Applications due for Youth Concerto Competition
TRANSP:OPAQUE
