BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Bloomington Symphony
DTSTART:20261101T220000Z
DTEND:20261101T233000Z
DTSTAMP:20261010T053048Z
UID:5860-1793552400-1793557800@www.bloomingtonsymphony.com
URL:https://www.bloomingtonsymphony.com/event/nov2026/
CREATED:20260928T203630Z
DESCRIPTION:Tickets Available Now\nAdults – $27\, Student – $14\, Children 
 under 18 – Free \nSunday\, Nov 1 2026\n4:15 pm pre-concert talk with compos
 er Gary Nash\n5:00 pm performance\nBuskirk-Chumley Theater\nGeneral Admissi
 on \n\nAmerica is a tune. It must be sung together. – Gerald Stanley Lee\, 
 Crowds: A Moving-Picture of Democracy\, 1913 \nOn Sunday\, November 1\, the
  Bloomington Symphony Orchestra\, in collaboration with the IU Archives of 
 African American Music and Culture\, will perform a concert in recognition 
 of our country’s 250th year. From the familiar square dance feel of Aaron C
 opland’s Hoedown to the soulful\, bluesy tonalities of William Grant Still’
 s Afro-American Symphony\, this concert explores what it means to be an Ame
 rican. \nProgram:\n“Hoedown” from Rodeo – Aaron Copland\n“In Memoriam Sojou
 rner Truth” – Gary Powell Nash\nAll Things Majestic – Jennifer Higdon\nSymp
 hony No. 1 – Afro-American Symphony – William Grant Still \nI travel the wo
 rld\, and I’m happy to say that America is still the great melting pot – ma
 ybe a chunky stew rather than a melting pot at this point\, but you know wh
 at I mean. – Philip Glass\, 1999 NPR interview \n\n\n\n\n\nBSO Season Passe
 s can be purchased through October 16th. Passes include discounted tickets 
 to all 4 season concerts\, reserved seating\, and other benefits. Learn mor
 e and purchase your Season Pass (CLICK HERE)\n\nTickets for this concert ar
 e available for purchase through the Buskirk-Chumley Theater Box Office onl
 ine\, or call 812-323-3020 ext 1\, or go to 114 E Kirkwood Ave.\n\n\n\n\n\n
 We don’t want cost to be the reason you don’t come to this concert. Thanks 
 to our generous donors\, we have some tickets available to ensure that anyb
 ody who wants to attend our concerts can do so\, regardless of their curren
 t financial situation. If you will use a ticket\, we will do all we can to 
 make you our guest. Fill out THIS SHORT FORM and we will contact you when w
 e have free tickets available.\n 
LAST-MODIFIED:20260929T014629Z
LOCATION:Buskirk-Chumley Theater\, 114 E. Kirkwood Avenue\, Bloomington\, I
 N\, 47408\, United States
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:We the People - Concert at Buskirk-Chumley Theater
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
